 61CO    50TI(14C,P2NG):XUNDL-4        2024AJ01                           202405
 61CO c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2024Aj01:                          
 61CO2c  Phys Rev C 109, 014305 (2024)                                          
 61CO c  Compiled by J. Chen (FRIB, MSU), January 31, 2024                      
 61CO c  2024Aj01: E=43 MeV {+14}C beam was produced from the 9-MV tandem       
 61CO2c  accelerator at the John D Fox Laboratory of Florida State University.  
 61CO3c  Target was a thin foil of {+50}Ti with a thickness of around 500       
 61CO4c  |mg/cm{+2} (>90% enriched). |g rays were detected with the FSU         
 61CO5c  |g-detector array of six HPGe clover detectors with three coupled to   
 61CO6c  BGO shields and three single-crystal Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,  
 61CO7c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(DCO), |g(lin pol). Deduced levels, J, |p, band         
 61CO8c  structures, |g-ray multipolarities. Comparisons with large-scale       
 61CO9c  shell-model calculations.                                              
 61CO cG $DCO values given under comments are for gate on quadrupole            
 61CO2cG transitions, unless otherwise noted.                                   
 61CO cG E,RI$From 2024Aj01                                                     
 61CO cG M$Deduced by 2024Aj01 based on measured |g|g(DCO) and |g(lin pol) data 
 61CO2cG as given under comments. Expected DCO values for gate on a pure dipole 
 61CO3cG transition are about 1.0 {I3} for pure dipole transitions and 1.85     
 61CO4cG {I35} for stretched quadrupole transitions; for gate on a stretched    
 61CO5cG quadrupole transitions DCO values are 0.55 {I15} and 1.05 {I25} for    
 61CO6cG dipole and quadrupole transitions, respectively. Positive POL value    
 61CO7cG indicates electric nature and negative value indicates magnetic nature 
 61CO8cG of a transition.                                                       
 61CO cG M(D)$DCO ratios for gate on dipole transitions.                        
 61CO cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies (by compiler)            
 61CO cL J$As given in 2024Aj01, based on measured |g|g(DCO), |g(lin pol) and   
 61CO2cL band assignments.                                                      
